{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1340313-electric-lich-legacy","id":1340313,"title":"Electric Lich Legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-08T15:55:58-07:00","id":1340313,"title":"Electric Lich Legacy","content":"I'm working on a Lich Legacy that transforms themselves into beings of living electricity, ripping the electrical pattern of their synapses from their body, expanding and transforming it into a body of lightning.<br /> <br /> My idea for their backstory is they got started in the late 18th century to early 19th century with the idea of Galvanism. The founder saw the Galvanism experiments that were happening at the time (basically electrocuting corpses to make them move), and became Obsessed with electricity and the idea it was the key to being &quot;alive&quot; without Life.<br /> <br /> My question is: Can the 5th Attainment permanently kill their body, by ripping every bit of energy from it, and give them a new body made of animate electricity (created from the energies taken from their original body), with Forces alone (no conjunctional Life or Mind)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-08-2019, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T17:41:51-07:00","id":1340328,"title":"","content":"The magic would say no, but an attainment can break some of the rules of magic, so go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T17:50:42-07:00","id":1340332,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it a minute, the more interesting question is why they want immortality. What\u2019re they doing with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T18:40:15-07:00","id":1340343,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking there is a schism in the Legacy between the members who still follow the original vision of the Legacy and a new branch (though not composed only of new members, some old members shifted their vision) formed in the 1980s who became obsessed with computers and the advancement of technology.<br /> <br /> The original vision focused on the eternal exploration of new mysteries. You can't investigate Mysteries if you are dead, and the founder and other early members found this end to the Mysteries to be unacceptable. They use their electric forms to travel as lightning bolts to far off places and explore mysteries that others would consider too far from civilization or too physically treacherous. They see the fact that Awakened society ostracizes liches to be a bonus, they can solve mysteries themselves that others have already solved without their conclusions being affected by others' findings. They are often nomadic; not settling down in one place and going where the Mysteries take them. They often attempt to recruit from the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> The new vision is similar in that they don't want to stop experiencing new things, but instead of focusing on Mysteries (although they love Mysteries just like any Mage), they are obsessed with the advance of technology (especially computers) and don't want to miss what's coming next. They are very much into futurism and transhumanism. They often use their electric powers and form to control and even enter computer systems. They are much less likely to be found away from civilization, because civilization is where the technology is. Although they fully split from the original branch in in 1980s, the beginnings of the philosophical split started a century earlier when some members became fascinated with the inventions of Tesla, Marconi, Edison, Bell, and others. They often attempt to recruit from the Free Council.<br /> <br /> Both branches are mechanically the same but with different philosophies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-08-2019, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T20:11:51-07:00","id":1340350,"title":"","content":"Cool. Do they think Ascension is a trap or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T20:24:31-07:00","id":1340353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1340313-electric-lich-legacy?p=1340350#post1340350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Do they think Ascension is a trap or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>That probably wouldn't be something they all agree on, but most would think Ascension is unachievable for the vast majority of mages, at least in a normal lifespan. Some may suspect that Ascension is some sort of static &quot;victory&quot; state, which is the opposite of what they want. Even if Ascension gives them omniscience and the answers to all the Mysteries, that's not what they want, its the opposite in fact. They want to keep discovering and experiencing new things forever, they would hate to have everything revealed for them at once. Running out of new things is pretty much their worst nightmare.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So overall few would be likely to pursue Ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-09-2019, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T23:58:46-07:00","id":1340374,"title":"","content":"I can respect that. I'm not as skeptical about the bennies of Ascension, but honestly it's all speculation so more power to them. At least they're not complete dickholes like most liches. I presume anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T09:13:27-07:00","id":1340424,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they are more about the love of discovery than the fear of death and accumulation of power.<br /> <br /> I wanted design a Legacy of Liches that were different from most and I had this idea of an almost jolly being of energy thats floating around looking at stuff, just having a fun time figuring things out. So I combined the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-09-2019, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T14:36:03-07:00","id":1340504,"title":"","content":"Unlike many Liches, they aren't running FROM death, they are running TOWARD an eternity of new experiences.<br /> <br /> Members of the new branch might try to recruit by saying something like: &quot;Are you disappointed that you were born too early to explore the stars? Why not stick around long enough to actually see that happen? We can show you how.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-09-2019, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T12:03:05-07:00","id":1340655,"title":"","content":"I think a Galvanism legacy would be cool, but I'm not sure if transforming your body permanently into electricity is actually a good way to overcome Death. It's not like electricity is naturally enduring or eternal, quite the contrary. The attainments can fudge the rules, but it still seems like a very counter intuitive idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe if they worked kind of like Prometheans, using large amounts of electricity to heal wounds and keep their bodies going beyond a normal life-span, even indefinitely, that would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T14:12:28-07:00","id":1340680,"title":"","content":"I'm still working on their Attainments, but their 4th Attainment is Perpetual Motion with indefinite duration which is used as part of their transformation, making their electric form potentially eternal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T22:40:10-07:00","id":1340735,"title":"","content":"If you haven't heard of &quot;A Madness of Angels: The Resurrection of Matthew Swift&quot; by Kate Griffin, go find yourself a copy. You'll like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}